1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:49,215
‎Pi-o, let's make a promise.

3
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:53,720
‎Let's play some more four hands
‎even after the competition.

4
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:54,637
‎Okay.

5
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,320
‎He left in the middle of the event,
‎went to a practice room,

6
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,322
‎and stared out the window
‎through the curtains.

7
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:19,746
‎He seemed very flustered when I walked in.

8
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:20,663
‎Could it be

9
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,374
‎that his memory is back?

10
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:36,012
‎Promise you won't sulk
‎if I win first place.

11
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,472
‎Let's still have fun when we hang out.

12
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,140
‎But I'm going to win first place.

13
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:40,600
‎Don't get sulky yourself.

14
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,159
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

15
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:01,162
‎EPISODE 10

16
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:45,248
‎Can I come in?

17
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:56,175
‎What brings you here at this hour?

18
00:02:58,887 --> 00:02:59,721
‎What is it?

19
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,223
‎Do you have a question about the piece?

20
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:04,225
‎Yeah.

21
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:06,102
‎What is it?

22
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,063
‎Still struggling with the tempo?

23
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:10,940
‎That piece.

24
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:13,735
‎You said you started writing it
‎five years ago, right?

25
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:16,529
‎It took me five years to finish.

26
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:17,655
‎Mr. Kang.

27
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:20,199
‎Please be the first to play this.

28
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:23,286
‎And your memory?

29
00:03:24,829 --> 00:03:26,873
‎You don't remember anything
‎after the accident?

30
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:28,791
‎That's right.

31
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:30,877
‎Why do you ask?

32
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:33,087
‎Is there a problem?

33
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,842
‎What did you mean
‎that I haven't changed at all?

34
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:42,805
‎Why haven't you changed at all, Mr. Kang?

35
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,933
‎Haven't changed since when?

36
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:46,559
‎Since high school?

37
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:48,686
‎Or since Prague?

38
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,564
‎What are you trying to say?

39
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:54,400
‎I'm asking how long you're planning
‎to keep up the amnesia act.

40
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:58,404
‎I don't understand what you're saying.

41
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,367
‎Then what about this?

42
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,495
‎When I was in your dorm
‎back in high school,

43
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,830
‎I saw a sketch you were working on.

44
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:08,790
‎But its subject

45
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,876
‎was the same as ‎Nemesis‎.

46
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:14,212
‎Really?

47
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:17,465
‎I composed something like that
‎in high school?

48
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:20,218
‎I guess

49
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:23,221
‎some mental images remain
‎even when you lose your memory.

50
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:26,266
‎Then…

51
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,603
‎how do you remember the practice room
‎where we first met?

52
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:32,981
‎Tell me.

53
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,275
‎Is that a coincidence as well?

54
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:42,115
‎Stop pretending, Choi Jeong-yo.

55
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,494
‎I know you remember everything.

56
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:52,709
‎Fine.

57
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:58,673
‎To be honest…

58
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:02,677
‎I've always wanted to visit

59
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,680
‎the practice room where we first met.

60
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:08,766
‎We played ‎Hungarian Dances…

61
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:11,394
‎and ‎Danse Macabre.

62
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:13,938
‎And then the noise in the hallway.

63
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,858
‎CHOI JEONG-YO WILL WIN 1ST PLACE
‎NOT TRUE, KANG PI-O WILL!

64
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:18,943
‎I've never once forgotten any of it.

65
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,279
‎Why did you do it?

66
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:26,117
‎Why did you tell such a lie?

67
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,160
‎You know why.

68
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,913
‎If I told you I remembered,

69
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:34,042
‎you would've tried to kill me again.

70
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,088
‎What are you talking about?

71
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:41,966
‎I would've tried to kill you again?

72
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,468
‎Don't play dumb.

73
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:45,595
‎I know you're the one

74
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:48,765
‎who ordered my abduction
‎at the competition nine years ago.

75
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,017
‎Don't even try to trick me.

76
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:55,897
‎I saw you meeting
‎one of my abductors with my own eyes.

77
00:05:57,356 --> 00:05:59,067
‎I couldn't believe it at first.

78
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,823
‎You were the friend I trusted
‎and depended on the most.

79
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:09,368
‎I never imagined you'd stoop so low.

80
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:14,916
‎Kang Pi-o.

81
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:16,250
‎He gave the order.

82
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:17,585
‎But then

83
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,922
‎I heard my abductor say your name.

84
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:25,051
‎Where's the nearest international bank?

85
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:27,845
‎What? You want to come back here?

86
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,435
‎Then I saw you hand over money
‎to another one.

87
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:37,480
‎I even went to your performances
‎several times.

88
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:38,648
‎But you…

89
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:42,276
‎You completely forgot I ever existed‎…

90
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:47,281
‎and kept performing
‎like nothing ever happened.

91
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,246
‎So, how has it been?

92
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,750
‎Did life feel easier
‎with me out of the picture?

93
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,795
‎Did it feel good to perform

94
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,338
‎as the winner?

95
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:16,352
‎Why did you do that to me?

96
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:21,023
‎No, I won't go!

97
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:22,400
‎I'd rather die

98
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,735
‎than let anyone know about this.

99
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:27,864
‎Are you willing to let me die like this?

100
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:43,463
‎I'm sorry.

101
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:47,717
‎You're right.

102
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,095
‎It was me.

103
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,519
‎It was the finals, and I hurt my finger.

104
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,896
‎I couldn't think straight.

105
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:02,607
‎I'd worked so hard to win the competition,

106
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,193
‎but I was afraid I couldn't win
‎because of you.

107
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,737
‎I'll turn myself in for what I did

108
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:10,698
‎and face the consequences.

109
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:13,367
‎I'll take responsibility

110
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,828
‎for everything.

111
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:17,705
‎"Responsibility"?

112
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:21,292
‎You completely ruined my life.

113
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,128
‎And you think
‎sitting pretty in a cell will cut it?

114
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:29,175
‎I didn't struggle to come back alive
‎just to give you a free pass.

115
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:31,052
‎Listen.

116
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:34,972
‎I'm the only one who gets to judge you.

117
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:37,934
‎And I'm the only one who gets to kill you.

118
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:40,645
‎If I just die, will this all end?

119
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:42,063
‎No.

120
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,358
‎I won't let it end that easily.

121
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:50,738
‎The second you take the easy way out,

122
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:53,324
‎the whole world will know what you did.

123
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:55,618
‎The same goes
‎for your accomplice of a mother.

124
00:08:58,412 --> 00:08:59,455
‎Just wait.

125
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,082
‎I'll show you what hell looks like.

126
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,337
‎It'll be more than
‎you can possibly imagine.

127
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:19,433
‎MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
‎TRADITIONAL MARKET

128
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:31,320
‎Hello.

129
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:34,156
‎Can I ask you a question?

130
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,408
‎By any chance,

131
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,910
‎do you know who this is?

132
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,329
‎He's Conductor Choi Jeong-yo,
‎and I hear he grew up here.

133
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,999
‎I think I've heard of him.

134
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:46,961
‎Then do you know
‎where Jeong-yo's father is?

135
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:48,838
‎I'm not sure.

136
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:51,841
‎Thank you anyway.

137
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,068
‎Excuse me.

138
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:13,863
‎Have you heard of Conductor Choi Jeong-yo?

139
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:18,075
‎I heard his father
‎used to work around here.

140
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,953
‎It's hard to say.

141
00:10:22,079 --> 00:10:24,248
‎He does look familiar,

142
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,085
‎but I could be wrong. I'm not sure.

143
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:30,546
‎I don't know.

144
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:39,430
‎Excuse me.

145
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,643
‎Are you looking for Choi Gi-taek?

146
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,153
‎Well…

147
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:55,613
‎May I ask your name?

148
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,406
‎Just call me Kim.

149
00:10:58,491 --> 00:10:59,325
‎And you?

150
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:01,744
‎Well,

151
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,288
‎I'm Jeong-yo's friend's mother.

152
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,457
‎I don't know if you've seen the news,

153
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,459
‎but Jeong-yo lost his memory.

154
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:12,713
‎I'm looking for his family,
‎hoping it might help him.

155
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:13,839
‎I see.

156
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,258
‎So you're trying to help?

157
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:19,595
‎So…

158
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,890
‎how do you know Jeong-yo?

159
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:25,017
‎I'm a close friend of his.

160
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,019
‎Right.

161
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,438
‎I see.

162
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,273
‎Then do you know

163
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,943
‎where Jeong-yo's father is?

164
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:36,153
‎The bastard who took off with my money?

165
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:38,697
‎I guess I could find him if I wanted to,

166
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,950
‎but he's probably
‎passed out drunk somewhere.

167
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:51,961
‎ALCOHOL REHAB CENTER

168
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:56,632
‎Oh, I…

169
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:01,554
‎I guess you don't know where he is either.

170
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:04,098
‎Thank you for your time.

171
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:05,808
‎If you'll excuse me.

172
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:20,990
‎You're Pianist Kang Pi-o's mother, right?

173
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:22,992
‎I saw the news then.

174
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:27,329
‎Jeong-yo went missing,
‎and Kang Pi-o won first place.

175
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,331
‎But you know,

176
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:32,084
‎word will get out
‎if you poke around like this.

177
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,508
‎Call me if you need any help.

178
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:54,231
‎Please pick up.

179
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:57,860
‎Pi-o.

180
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:58,777
‎Yes?

181
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:00,279
‎What are we going to do?

182
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:02,823
‎Choi Jeong-yo

183
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,784
‎doesn't have amnesia.

184
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:08,829
‎His father is an alcoholic.

185
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:10,956
‎He was at that alcohol rehab center.

186
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:12,875
‎He…

187
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:16,504
‎He's trying to get revenge on us.
‎What should we do?

188
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:19,173
‎He'll expose us if we do nothing.

189
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:22,551
‎We need to stop him somehow.

190
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,428
‎We have to, no matter what!

191
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:25,971
‎How would we do that?

192
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,057
‎We committed a crime,

193
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:30,643
‎and he'd only be telling the truth.

194
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:33,687
‎We need to get rid of him
‎so he can't talk.

195
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,189
‎What are you saying?

196
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:37,316
‎We have no choice if we want to survive!

197
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:38,901
‎Just stop it!

198
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,987
‎If you go after Jeong-yo again…

199
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:45,866
‎I swear I won't just stand by.

200
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:46,909
‎Have you lost your mind?

201
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,119
‎Don't you understand?

202
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:52,998
‎He came back to get revenge on us!

203
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,583
‎Then I'll let him…

204
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,378
‎take out his revenge on me.

205
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:58,295
‎Pi-o!

206
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:08,180
‎This contract contains
‎too many toxic clauses for our soloist.

207
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:10,599
‎Under these terms,

208
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,644
‎he will have to take on too much risk
‎if the project falls through.

209
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:17,606
‎We're also taking a risk
‎by signing this contract.

210
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:21,527
‎Recording a world premiere is different
‎from recording standard repertoire.

211
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:24,905
‎Still, this is too much.

212
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:28,033
‎This soloist replacement clause is--

213
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,410
‎I'm sure you know

214
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:32,872
‎that's just a safeguard
‎against a worst-case scenario.

215
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:35,291
‎If the recording gets delayed
‎because of the soloist,

216
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,543
‎it will disrupt the schedules

217
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,753
‎for the orchestra and the engineers.

218
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,297
‎We're just trying to minimize the damage.

219
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,132
‎To be honest,

220
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,926
‎our partners overseas

221
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:49,263
‎have expressed their concerns
‎about Mr. Kang…

222
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,684
‎We understand your position.

223
00:14:53,767 --> 00:14:56,645
‎We'll discuss this further internally.

224
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:12,828
‎Why did you do that?

225
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:15,581
‎You should've had them
‎remove the toxic clauses first.

226
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:16,540
‎What's the rush?

227
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:21,170
‎Don't worry.
‎It'll be fine if I just play well.

228
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,255
‎There's no time.

229
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:27,009
‎Once the schedule is set,

230
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:29,261
‎I'll send you a list of ‎tonmeisters‎.

231
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:33,223
‎We definitely plan to book Dominic
‎since he's the best in the industry,

232
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,975
‎but in case he's unavailable,

233
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,729
‎I'll have a backup list ready.

234
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,773
‎Well done.

235
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:44,985
‎Now that the contract is signed,
‎I'm feeling nervous.

236
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:48,405
‎On that note, let's increase
‎your individual practice time.

237
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:51,784
‎The orchestra is coming together,

238
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:54,662
‎but I'm worried about the solo part.

239
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:57,581
‎What do you say?

240
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,000
‎Can you make some time?

241
00:16:00,918 --> 00:16:02,044
‎I will.

242
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:05,005
‎We need to work on the details,

243
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,549
‎so come alone without the accompanist.

244
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:11,220
‎I'm counting on you.

245
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,029
‎So…

246
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,657
‎what's going to happen to us?

247
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:37,246
‎Do we just wait until our lives are over?

248
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:39,456
‎I'll do whatever I can,

249
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:42,793
‎so don't worry.

250
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,025
‎Come in.

251
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,171
‎Wait.

252
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,340
‎At this tempo.

253
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,009
‎But why?

254
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:36,263
‎The opening should focus on
‎evoking an emotional response,

255
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,557
‎not the speed.

256
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:42,686
‎You think your opinion matters right now?

257
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,940
‎I have a specific sound and tempo in mind.

258
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:50,152
‎But you completely lack the power
‎to express that.

259
00:17:50,235 --> 00:17:51,320
‎I want this piece

260
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:54,573
‎to erupt with explosive cohesion.

261
00:17:55,532 --> 00:17:58,118
‎I don't want a weak and limp delivery.

262
00:17:58,202 --> 00:17:59,036
‎Understand?

263
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,339
‎Again.

264
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:54,883
‎Play the cadenza at this tempo.

265
00:18:55,634 --> 00:18:57,386
‎What are you trying to pull here?

266
00:18:58,095 --> 00:18:58,929
‎What is it?

267
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:01,181
‎Trying to ruin my tendons
‎so I can't play anymore?

268
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,725
‎Is this the revenge
‎you told me to wait for?

269
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,686
‎Do you still not get it?

270
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:11,692
‎You've got this all wrong.

271
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,280
‎I didn't give you my precious music

272
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,574
‎to waste on some petty scheme.

273
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:26,248
‎I had a gun aimed at my head.

274
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:34,381
‎The car drove deep into a forest.

275
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:36,341
‎It was obvious what they were up to.

276
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:40,262
‎To take me somewhere isolated
‎and kill me without anyone knowing.

277
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:43,307
‎Watch it before you drive us into a grave.

278
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,308
‎No, you watch it.

279
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,185
‎Don't get blood splatter in the car.

280
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:50,063
‎Then I saw an opening to get out alive.

281
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,107
‎They started fighting.

282
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:55,777
‎I saw that as my chance
‎and fought for my life to get away.

283
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:58,989
‎I thought I'd made it.

284
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:00,991
‎I thought I was free.

285
00:20:01,658 --> 00:20:02,868
‎But I was wrong.

286
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:04,536
‎Just then,

287
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:09,708
‎I heard a bullet
‎rip through my right shoulder.

288
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,050
‎The shock of it…

289
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,803
‎left me with no memory for five years…

290
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,806
‎until I saw you again.

291
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:27,851
‎That very moment.

292
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:32,397
‎I wrote that hellish moment
‎into the cadenza.

293
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:34,733
‎So do you really think

294
00:20:35,984 --> 00:20:39,196
‎you're delivering that overwhelming fear
‎in your performance?

295
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,699
‎Don't kid yourself.

296
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:45,953
‎I'm not doing this to screw you over.

297
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,081
‎Making ‎Nemesis‎ into a masterpiece

298
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:50,916
‎matters more to me than to you.

299
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,000
‎So…

300
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:56,171
‎instead of worrying about
‎pulling a stupid tendon…

301
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:02,302
‎think about whether you're capturing
‎the vision of the composer.

302
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:07,099
‎You expect me to forgive you
‎with that kind of complacent attitude?

303
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,205
‎Fourth and fifth fingers are weak.

304
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:33,917
‎With more clarity!

305
00:22:52,579 --> 00:22:54,331
‎I have to keep going.

306
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:21,733
‎You failed to satisfy me today.

307
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:25,987
‎The cadenza isn't as murderous
‎and hostile as it should be.

308
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:53,765
‎How is the schedule for the concert hall?

309
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:57,978
‎I checked,
‎and the venue was fully booked,

310
00:23:58,061 --> 00:23:59,521
‎but I managed to secure a day.

311
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:02,023
‎Will a day be enough?

312
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:04,484
‎I'm afraid the schedule will be too tight.

313
00:24:04,568 --> 00:24:08,989
‎Jeong-yo is working tirelessly with Pi-o
‎and the orchestra in separate rehearsals,

314
00:24:09,072 --> 00:24:11,491
‎so doing it all in one day
‎shouldn't be a problem.

315
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:13,451
‎We can record the movements
‎separately that day,

316
00:24:13,535 --> 00:24:14,995
‎so it should be fine.

317
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:16,621
‎Separate rehearsals?

318
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:17,706
‎Yes.

319
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:20,333
‎But why separate rehearsals?

320
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:21,251
‎I don't know.

321
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:24,880
‎Jeong-yo says it's too early
‎to bring them together.

322
00:24:25,505 --> 00:24:26,923
‎He's been fine-tuning them separately.

323
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:30,177
‎I'm sure the composer knows
‎what he's doing.

324
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:36,183
‎Why are you letting mere finger pain
‎dull your playing?

325
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,150
‎Don't make a fuss and focus until the end!

326
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:51,239
‎What the hell, Choi Jeong-yo?

327
00:24:53,116 --> 00:24:55,118
‎How can you talk to an artist like that?

328
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:56,203
‎Jae-in.

329
00:24:58,079 --> 00:24:58,955
‎What are you doing?

330
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:00,248
‎What's with the tempo?

331
00:25:00,832 --> 00:25:02,209
‎Why is he playing so fast?

332
00:25:02,292 --> 00:25:04,252
‎You know that will ruin his fingers.

333
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:06,129
‎What's wrong with you?

334
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:08,006
‎Come on, let's talk outside.

335
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:12,427
‎Pi-o.

336
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:13,678
‎What's wrong with your hands?

337
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:21,269
‎Hey, Choi Jeong-yo.

338
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:23,647
‎What do you think you're doing?

339
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:27,400
‎If his hands were that bad,
‎you should've told him to rest!

340
00:25:27,901 --> 00:25:29,861
‎What if he can't play the piano anymore?

341
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:31,238
‎Will you take responsibility?

342
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,532
‎Follow me out right now.

343
00:25:34,616 --> 00:25:35,575
‎Let go of me.

344
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:36,868
‎I said let go!

345
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:45,835
‎Tell me.

346
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,923
‎What's his problem with you?

347
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:52,133
‎And why are you just sitting back?

348
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:53,927
‎Did you do something wrong?

349
00:25:54,552 --> 00:25:56,638
‎Whether I ruin my fingers
‎or the performance,

350
00:25:57,555 --> 00:25:58,598
‎that's my problem.

351
00:25:58,682 --> 00:26:00,809
‎So stay out of my business.

352
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:02,060
‎Listen, Kang Pi-o.

353
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:06,731
‎My job comes before our relationship.

354
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:11,403
‎You're in no state to record or perform.

355
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:12,946
‎So I can't stay out of it.

356
00:26:13,446 --> 00:26:14,489
‎This won't do.

357
00:26:15,448 --> 00:26:18,076
‎You need to push back the recording.

358
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:21,579
‎Actually, just don't do
‎the performance at all.

359
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:24,082
‎The company will pay the penalty fee,

360
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:25,959
‎so cancel the contract.

361
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:31,589
‎I can't get past how controlling
‎Choi Jeong-yo has been with you

362
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,134
‎and how strange his training methods are.

363
00:26:34,217 --> 00:26:36,928
‎I don't know what his musical vision is,

364
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:39,055
‎and he's nitpicking for no reason.

365
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:42,183
‎He may be the composer, but what the hell?

366
00:26:43,143 --> 00:26:44,144
‎At this rate,

367
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,479
‎both of you will go down.

368
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:47,605
‎You'll both go down, so--

369
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:48,898
‎That's enough!

370
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:52,986
‎Why do you keep crossing the line
‎when I said I'd take care of it?

371
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:04,372
‎Look, I'm sorry.

372
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:08,251
‎But I have to do this performance
‎no matter what.

373
00:27:09,961 --> 00:27:11,296
‎So stay out of it.

374
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:14,758
‎If there's a problem
‎or I ruin the performance,

375
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:17,385
‎I'll take full responsibility.

376
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:19,804
‎Okay?

377
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:33,818
‎I'm the only one who gets to judge you.

378
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:37,822
‎And I'm the only one who gets to kill you.

379
00:27:38,656 --> 00:27:39,783
‎Just wait.

380
00:27:39,866 --> 00:27:41,326
‎I'll show you what hell looks like.

381
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:49,125
‎Jae-in, let's meet up tomorrow.

382
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:50,418
‎I need to tell you something.

383
00:27:51,586 --> 00:27:52,837
‎I'll go to your neighborhood.

384
00:27:53,338 --> 00:27:55,298
‎JAE-IN, LET'S MEET UP TOMORROW.

385
00:27:57,592 --> 00:28:00,095
‎I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING.
‎I'LL GO TO YOUR NEIGHBORHOOD.

386
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,774
‎So? What do you need to tell me?

387
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:17,362
‎What is it?

388
00:28:19,447 --> 00:28:20,573
‎Are you here to apologize?

389
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,869
‎Is that why you can't even look at me?

390
00:28:27,497 --> 00:28:28,498
‎It's okay.

391
00:28:28,581 --> 00:28:29,999
‎I understand.

392
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:35,130
‎I know you get on edge
‎before a performance.

393
00:28:36,881 --> 00:28:40,927
‎But it hurt when you said
‎I crossed the line.

394
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:50,019
‎How are your hands?

395
00:28:51,771 --> 00:28:56,401
‎Why are you so obsessed
‎with Jeong-yo's piece?

396
00:28:57,152 --> 00:28:58,570
‎Why push yourself so hard?

397
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:01,489
‎Did something happen between you two?

398
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:03,366
‎Jae-in.

399
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:08,455
‎I asked to see you today because…

400
00:29:13,793 --> 00:29:15,086
‎I think we should break up.

401
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:22,385
‎I want to focus on music,
‎but you keep getting in the way.

402
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:25,013
‎And when I ask myself

403
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:28,016
‎whether we started dating
‎because I really liked you…

404
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:31,603
‎I don't think that's the case.

405
00:29:34,814 --> 00:29:36,858
‎You're always trying to control me…

406
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:40,069
‎and it's suffocating.

407
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:45,074
‎I know it sounds irresponsible of me,

408
00:29:46,493 --> 00:29:48,703
‎but I felt you deserved my honesty.

409
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,457
‎I'm sorry…

410
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,085
‎for hurting you like this.

411
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:00,799
‎I'll get going.

412
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:19,567
‎What's wrong with you?

413
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:22,737
‎So this is it?

414
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:25,698
‎You just say your piece, and it's over?

415
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:29,577
‎You're right.

416
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:32,288
‎We're dating,
‎but our feelings weren't mutual.

417
00:30:32,997 --> 00:30:33,915
‎I admit it.

418
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:38,670
‎But you've treated me
‎like someone special since childhood.

419
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,047
‎No, I just…

420
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:44,759
‎I just needed someone to support me.

421
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:47,136
‎Fine.

422
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:50,265
‎Just tell me this.

423
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:54,686
‎Did you…

424
00:30:57,939 --> 00:30:59,232
‎even for a single moment…

425
00:31:00,316 --> 00:31:01,776
‎ever love me?

426
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:04,445
‎No.

427
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:05,780
‎Never.

428
00:31:14,539 --> 00:31:15,582
‎Not even once?

429
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:24,924
‎I'm sorry.

430
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:07,592
‎EUGENE ART CENTER

431
00:33:37,724 --> 00:33:39,600
‎Okay, let's begin recording.

432
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:41,310
‎Take one.

433
00:34:54,675 --> 00:34:55,676
‎Take two.

434
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,349
‎What's the issue this time?

435
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:46,144
‎I don't think there was any issue.

436
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:48,312
‎No, there was an issue.

437
00:35:50,189 --> 00:35:53,401
‎Others might not have felt it,
‎but I felt it clearly.

438
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:56,445
‎A hint of your unease.

439
00:36:01,576 --> 00:36:02,451
‎Understood.

440
00:36:03,035 --> 00:36:04,912
‎You probably feel rushed and anxious,

441
00:36:04,996 --> 00:36:07,290
‎but try to relax and play comfortably.

442
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:11,836
‎After all, if you can't pull this off,
‎none of us are going home.

443
00:36:14,046 --> 00:36:15,173
‎Let's go home, okay?

444
00:36:21,345 --> 00:36:22,346
‎Take three.

445
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:08,267
‎This isn't it.

446
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:11,520
‎The tension needs to peak right here,

447
00:37:12,104 --> 00:37:12,980
‎but it's too loose.

448
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:16,567
‎I played with as much intensity
‎as I could!

449
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:18,986
‎No.

450
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:23,032
‎You only moved your fingers
‎as quickly as you could.

451
00:37:23,616 --> 00:37:26,452
‎The emotional intensity
‎never once hit its peak.

452
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:30,665
‎Look here.

453
00:37:31,249 --> 00:37:33,042
‎What do you think is my intention here?

454
00:37:33,125 --> 00:37:35,461
‎I expressed the mounting terror
‎of death closing in

455
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:38,089
‎through eighth notes,
‎sixteenth notes, and triplets.

456
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:39,590
‎And here!

457
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:45,554
‎This is written in marcato to convey
‎a sense of betrayal and vengeance.

458
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:46,555
‎So…

459
00:37:47,598 --> 00:37:51,269
‎Do you really think
‎you're capturing any of these emotions?

460
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,853
‎No, you're not!

461
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:59,944
‎Do you want to run off
‎from the weight of these emotions?

462
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:01,862
‎I told you, didn't I?

463
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:04,156
‎To capture and express
‎the scenery I saw

464
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:07,576
‎and the emotions I felt with precision.

465
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:11,956
‎Right now,
‎all you're doing is running away.

466
00:38:13,374 --> 00:38:15,835
‎Stop avoiding it and face it!

467
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:21,299
‎Stop being a burden to everyone here

468
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,635
‎and attack it head-on.

469
00:38:25,594 --> 00:38:27,805
‎I truly hope you'll pull it off this time.

470
00:38:27,888 --> 00:38:29,432
‎Stop running away.

471
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:35,563
‎Take 27.

472
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:53,998
‎I just wanted the best for you.

473
00:38:55,082 --> 00:38:56,959
‎It was for you.

474
00:38:57,043 --> 00:38:59,045
‎Stop talking nonsense!

475
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:16,145
‎You know.

476
00:39:16,228 --> 00:39:19,732
‎I'm talking about
‎that nasty rumor about you

477
00:39:19,815 --> 00:39:21,650
‎being involved in Jeong-yo's abduction.

478
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,779
‎By the way,
‎about that Choi Jeong-yo rumor…

479
00:39:24,862 --> 00:39:26,280
‎What's the deal with that?

480
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:28,324
‎People say you were behind it.

481
00:39:58,187 --> 00:39:59,105
‎What is it?

482
00:40:01,607 --> 00:40:03,317
‎Have your fingers given out?

483
00:40:05,486 --> 00:40:06,529
‎They just…

484
00:40:07,029 --> 00:40:08,531
‎I did worry this might happen, but…

485
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:13,202
‎It's my fault
‎for overestimating your competence.

486
00:40:14,161 --> 00:40:16,580
‎And it was my mistake
‎for giving you this piece.

487
00:40:17,456 --> 00:40:19,166
‎As of today, you're out.

488
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:23,129
‎Everyone.

489
00:40:24,213 --> 00:40:25,339
‎I'm very sorry.

490
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:27,174
‎Today's recording is canceled.

491
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:42,773
‎I'm sorry. We'll take a short break.

492
00:40:58,497 --> 00:40:59,540
‎Hey.

493
00:41:00,791 --> 00:41:02,626
‎This was your plan all along, wasn't it?

494
00:41:02,710 --> 00:41:05,796
‎Go ahead and expose me
‎instead of toying with me like this.

495
00:41:06,464 --> 00:41:08,591
‎I'll take whatever punishment
‎and get out of your sight.

496
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:11,051
‎So just expose me, you bastard!

497
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:15,097
‎You didn't know I'd do this?

498
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:17,183
‎I told you.

499
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:20,227
‎I'm going to make you feel
‎every bit of pain, rage, and betrayal

500
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,855
‎that I went through.

501
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:29,195
‎But you know,

502
00:41:29,945 --> 00:41:32,740
‎I'm a little disappointed in you,
‎Kang Pi-o.

503
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:37,369
‎I was curious to see
‎if you could push past this limit.

504
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:39,413
‎And to be honest…

505
00:41:40,831 --> 00:41:42,124
‎I was hoping you would.

506
00:41:48,088 --> 00:41:49,006
‎This just proves

507
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,384
‎you're nothing but a pathetic loser

508
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:55,262
‎who should've never pursued music
‎in the first place.

509
00:41:56,138 --> 00:41:59,892
‎Jealous bastards like you
‎destroy real geniuses.

510
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:08,025
‎How dare a mediocre pianist like you

511
00:42:09,109 --> 00:42:12,404
‎try to cheat your way to the top
‎by killing me?

512
00:42:14,782 --> 00:42:15,699
‎Hey.

513
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:22,581
‎You'll never beat me.

514
00:42:33,008 --> 00:42:33,842
‎Pi-o.

515
00:42:34,593 --> 00:42:35,553
‎Pi-o.

516
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:39,181
‎Give me the key right now.

517
00:42:39,265 --> 00:42:40,266
‎Hurry!

518
00:42:50,442 --> 00:42:51,402
‎Pi-o.

519
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:07,501
‎Why didn't you listen to me?

520
00:43:11,714 --> 00:43:12,965
‎Look at your hands.

521
00:43:16,719 --> 00:43:18,262
‎I'm sorry.

522
00:43:18,345 --> 00:43:22,016
‎I tried to communicate my vision
‎as the composer to Pianist Kang Pi-o,

523
00:43:22,099 --> 00:43:23,183
‎but it proved rather difficult.

524
00:43:23,684 --> 00:43:26,228
‎I should've altered course earlier, but…

525
00:43:27,187 --> 00:43:28,439
‎This is all on me.

526
00:43:28,522 --> 00:43:29,440
‎I'm not sure.

527
00:43:30,649 --> 00:43:31,775
‎Was Kang Pi-o

528
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:34,528
‎the real problem here?

529
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:35,654
‎The way I see it,

530
00:43:36,322 --> 00:43:40,826
‎the issue was your poor communication
‎rattling the soloist.

531
00:43:41,910 --> 00:43:45,122
‎The rehearsals were unnecessarily brutal,
‎and you put him through verbal abuse.

532
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:47,541
‎That's why he lost his nerve

533
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:49,126
‎and broke down.

534
00:43:49,209 --> 00:43:50,794
‎Hong Jae-in, stop right now.

535
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:55,007
‎The soloist just wasn't strong enough
‎to master the piece.

536
00:43:55,090 --> 00:43:56,967
‎Don't blame the composer.

537
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:57,968
‎Ms. Han.

538
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:03,307
‎This means Pi-o
‎didn't fully get over his slump.

539
00:44:04,558 --> 00:44:06,977
‎We were too caught up
‎in our recent success,

540
00:44:07,061 --> 00:44:08,896
‎so we failed to see that.

541
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:10,481
‎That's not true.

542
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:13,734
‎He played really well from where I stood.

543
00:44:15,527 --> 00:44:16,737
‎Whatever the case,

544
00:44:18,113 --> 00:44:19,156
‎Pi-o is the one

545
00:44:19,948 --> 00:44:23,452
‎who ruined an expensive recording session.

546
00:44:24,620 --> 00:44:27,539
‎No matter how well he plays offstage,
‎if he can't stay composed on stage,

547
00:44:27,623 --> 00:44:29,124
‎that alone

548
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:30,959
‎means he's not qualified.

549
00:44:32,461 --> 00:44:35,798
‎The 80th anniversary concert
‎is right around the corner.

550
00:44:35,881 --> 00:44:37,174
‎Never mind the album.

551
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:39,343
‎What will you do about the performance?

552
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:42,137
‎I thought something like this
‎might happen,

553
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:44,890
‎so I kept someone in mind as a backup.

554
00:44:46,183 --> 00:44:48,310
‎How do you feel about
‎Pianist Lee Min-sung?

555
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:50,521
‎Lee Min-sung…

556
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:54,650
‎Lee Min-sung…

557
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:00,239
‎JAE-IN

558
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:06,078
‎KANG PI-O REPLACED BY PIANIST LEE MIN-SUNG

559
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:14,253
‎KANG PI-O REPLACED BY PIANIST LEE MIN-SUNG

560
00:45:14,336 --> 00:45:15,671
‎KANG HAD DIFFICULTY DURING REHEARSAL…

561
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:27,015
‎I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

562
00:45:27,099 --> 00:45:31,186
‎As you warned me, Pianist Kang Pi-o
‎wasn't the right fit for this piece.

563
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:33,564
‎But I was being stubborn.

564
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:35,482
‎I apologize for the worry I've caused.

565
00:45:37,359 --> 00:45:39,862
‎If that's what the composer says,
‎I guess that's how it is.

566
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:41,613
‎However,

567
00:45:42,197 --> 00:45:45,534
‎do you remember
‎what I said about that piece?

568
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:51,415
‎I hoped it would be performed
‎as music that speaks to everyone.

569
00:45:52,458 --> 00:45:54,293
‎Did you try to make that happen?

570
00:45:56,170 --> 00:45:57,337
‎You see,

571
00:45:58,088 --> 00:46:01,967
‎I get the sense
‎that your intentions weren't so pure.

572
00:46:02,551 --> 00:46:03,886
‎Why is that?

573
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:04,970
‎I'm not sure.

574
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:10,476
‎I only wrote the best piece I could.

575
00:46:18,650 --> 00:46:19,651
‎Here.

576
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:25,616
‎I'm sorry for dropping by unannounced.

577
00:46:28,702 --> 00:46:31,788
‎But I'm just so frustrated.

578
00:46:32,706 --> 00:46:34,333
‎And I have no one to talk to.

579
00:46:35,459 --> 00:46:37,419
‎Don't worry about it. It's okay.

580
00:46:37,503 --> 00:46:39,296
‎Go ahead and tell me everything.

581
00:46:41,507 --> 00:46:42,424
‎I'm sure

582
00:46:43,550 --> 00:46:45,469
‎something happened between them.

583
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:47,262
‎I saw Jeong-yo

584
00:46:47,971 --> 00:46:50,390
‎deliberately being brutal to Pi-o

585
00:46:51,433 --> 00:46:53,352
‎with my own eyes.

586
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:56,730
‎And Pi-o is keeping his mouth shut

587
00:46:57,314 --> 00:46:58,649
‎for whatever reason.

588
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:02,236
‎Since Jeong-yo is the conductor
‎and the composer,

589
00:47:02,319 --> 00:47:07,241
‎-it's natural for him to get ambitious--
‎-I understand that much.

590
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:11,119
‎But it all feels very personal.

591
00:47:14,456 --> 00:47:15,332
‎It's like…

592
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:20,170
‎he's determined to bring Pi-o down.

593
00:47:24,466 --> 00:47:26,301
‎Please save Pi-o.

594
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:30,806
‎Please get Choi Jeong-yo away from Pi-o.

595
00:47:30,889 --> 00:47:32,307
‎I'm so scared.

596
00:47:33,642 --> 00:47:35,352
‎I'm scared to death.

597
00:47:44,486 --> 00:47:46,029
‎Call me if you need any help.

598
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:54,454
‎PERSONAL CONSULTING SERVICES
‎KIM SE-JIN

599
00:47:56,915 --> 00:47:58,375
‎HYUN-SOO

600
00:48:03,797 --> 00:48:04,840
‎Hello?

601
00:48:04,923 --> 00:48:06,883
‎Where are you right now? Let's talk.

602
00:48:06,967 --> 00:48:08,385
‎I'm busy. Can we do this later--

603
00:48:08,468 --> 00:48:10,470
‎This concerns Pi-o. We need to talk.

604
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:21,273
‎What's this about?

605
00:48:22,441 --> 00:48:24,735
‎Is it about Pi-o being removed
‎from the concerto?

606
00:48:25,861 --> 00:48:27,779
‎Choi Jeong-yo was playing games with him.

607
00:48:28,572 --> 00:48:30,073
‎And Pi-o fell for it.

608
00:48:31,033 --> 00:48:31,867
‎Why?

609
00:48:35,162 --> 00:48:37,539
‎Why would Jeong-yo play games with Pi-o?

610
00:48:39,082 --> 00:48:39,958
‎I don't know.

611
00:48:41,460 --> 00:48:45,339
‎He probably thought Pi-o's life
‎was all roses while he was missing.

612
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:49,468
‎Jealousy of sorts, perhaps?

613
00:48:49,551 --> 00:48:51,762
‎You know that's not what it is, Ji-hye.

614
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:54,139
‎Come on, you know it's not!

615
00:48:56,850 --> 00:49:00,979
‎Please just tell me the truth
‎about what happened back then.

616
00:49:01,063 --> 00:49:03,482
‎That nasty rumor that went around.

617
00:49:03,565 --> 00:49:06,735
‎The one about Pi-o being involved
‎in Jeong-yo's disappearance.

618
00:49:06,818 --> 00:49:08,528
‎Was that actually true?

619
00:49:09,696 --> 00:49:10,739
‎How could you say that?

620
00:49:13,408 --> 00:49:14,242
‎It's not true.

621
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:20,332
‎How could you believe
‎a ridiculous rumor like that?

622
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:24,086
‎I'm leaving.

623
00:49:25,671 --> 00:49:27,589
‎Then what did you mean before?

624
00:49:28,548 --> 00:49:31,385
‎You asked me
‎to get Jeong-yo away from Pi-o!

625
00:49:31,968 --> 00:49:33,553
‎You said you were scared to death!

626
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:35,555
‎What the hell did you mean by that?

627
00:49:44,272 --> 00:49:45,190
‎This just proves

628
00:49:45,941 --> 00:49:47,984
‎you're nothing but a pathetic loser

629
00:49:48,652 --> 00:49:51,363
‎who should've never pursued music
‎in the first place.

630
00:49:52,906 --> 00:49:56,451
‎Jealous bastards like you
‎destroy real geniuses.

631
00:50:04,167 --> 00:50:05,001
‎No.

632
00:50:07,879 --> 00:50:09,798
‎Pi-o didn't do anything.

633
00:50:09,881 --> 00:50:10,716
‎Pi-o…

634
00:50:12,426 --> 00:50:13,552
‎He's innocent.

635
00:50:14,594 --> 00:50:15,512
‎It was all me…

636
00:50:17,556 --> 00:50:18,515
‎It was me.

637
00:50:20,559 --> 00:50:21,768
‎I did it.

638
00:50:24,521 --> 00:50:25,564
‎I…

639
00:50:27,899 --> 00:50:29,276
‎I did it.

640
00:52:14,089 --> 00:52:15,298
‎Grandfather.

641
00:52:16,591 --> 00:52:17,801
‎Is it agonizing?

642
00:52:29,938 --> 00:52:32,023
‎That's the nature of art.

643
00:52:35,318 --> 00:52:37,737
‎It'd be easier to reach for the stars.

644
00:52:39,322 --> 00:52:41,283
‎Art is like a mirage.

645
00:52:42,033 --> 00:52:44,828
‎You chase it down,
‎only for it to move farther away.

646
00:52:44,911 --> 00:52:47,747
‎When you pursue it again,
‎it moves even farther.

647
00:52:52,335 --> 00:52:55,380
‎Do you still want to
‎go down this thorny road?

648
00:52:58,008 --> 00:53:01,219
‎If you had less than a month to live,

649
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:04,180
‎would you still want to play the piano?

650
00:53:16,651 --> 00:53:17,485
‎Yes.

651
00:53:18,153 --> 00:53:19,321
‎I would.

652
00:53:20,739 --> 00:53:22,574
‎I know I don't have what it takes…

653
00:53:24,993 --> 00:53:26,828
‎but I'm only happy when I play the piano.

654
00:53:28,204 --> 00:53:29,122
‎Even if…

655
00:53:30,624 --> 00:53:32,375
‎Even if I only had one day left to live,

656
00:53:33,919 --> 00:53:35,462
‎I'd still want to play the piano.

657
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:30,517
‎Break the mold, Pi-o.

658
00:54:31,267 --> 00:54:33,812
‎Stop relying on that chunk of metal,

659
00:54:33,895 --> 00:54:36,439
‎and find your own inner rhythm.

660
00:54:41,111 --> 00:54:44,447
‎For a soloist,
‎confidence is half the battle.

661
00:54:45,281 --> 00:54:47,659
‎Command the stage with your energy.

662
00:54:47,742 --> 00:54:48,994
‎If your energy is strong enough,

663
00:54:49,786 --> 00:54:54,332
‎you can pull the conductor
‎and the orchestra into your orbit.

664
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:00,755
‎Looking back,

665
00:55:01,548 --> 00:55:04,551
‎I've realized that music
‎that moves people's hearts

666
00:55:04,634 --> 00:55:07,345
‎is one that carries a lifetime within it.

667
00:55:08,722 --> 00:55:09,889
‎So…

668
00:55:10,473 --> 00:55:13,143
‎you said you wanted to play
‎even if you only had one day to live.

669
00:55:13,226 --> 00:55:15,061
‎Pour that resolve and your life

670
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:18,815
‎into your music.

671
00:55:32,162 --> 00:55:33,246
‎Do you understand?

672
00:55:52,307 --> 00:55:53,183
‎Mr. Choi.

673
00:55:54,017 --> 00:55:55,310
‎Please say hello.

674
00:55:55,393 --> 00:55:59,064
‎We managed to get Pianist Lee Min-sung
‎for your premiere piece.

675
00:55:59,647 --> 00:56:00,899
‎Hello.

676
00:56:00,982 --> 00:56:02,609
‎It's an honor to meet you.

677
00:56:02,692 --> 00:56:03,818
‎The honor is mine.

678
00:56:03,902 --> 00:56:05,945
‎Thank you for agreeing
‎to play the concerto.

679
00:56:06,029 --> 00:56:06,905
‎Please, sit.

680
00:56:10,033 --> 00:56:12,786
‎There wasn't much time,
‎so I could only practice a little.

681
00:56:13,411 --> 00:56:15,371
‎Shall I go ahead and play?

682
00:56:15,455 --> 00:56:16,331
‎Yes, please.

683
00:56:17,499 --> 00:56:18,666
‎It's all right.

684
00:57:24,023 --> 00:57:25,567
‎This is that woman's photo.

685
00:57:26,734 --> 00:57:27,569
‎And this…

686
00:57:28,945 --> 00:57:29,821
‎I'm sorry.

687
00:57:31,489 --> 00:57:32,407
‎You're right.

688
00:57:33,741 --> 00:57:34,742
‎It was me.

689
00:57:35,326 --> 00:57:37,704
‎It was the finals, and I hurt my finger.

690
00:57:37,787 --> 00:57:39,080
‎I couldn't think straight.

691
00:57:39,914 --> 00:57:42,083
‎I'd worked so hard to win the competition,

692
00:57:42,167 --> 00:57:44,377
‎but I was afraid I couldn't win
‎because of you.

693
00:57:49,716 --> 00:57:50,717
‎COPYING FILES

694
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:53,178
‎KANG PI-O
‎KANG JI-HYE

695
00:57:53,761 --> 00:57:56,764
‎Now we have the files we need
‎to bury the two.

696
00:57:58,057 --> 00:57:58,933
‎So?

697
00:57:59,017 --> 00:58:00,602
‎You already broke him mentally,

698
00:58:00,685 --> 00:58:02,228
‎so we just release it all at once, right?

699
00:58:03,062 --> 00:58:03,897
‎Right?

700
00:58:06,941 --> 00:58:08,526
‎Sure, let's do that.

701
00:58:10,195 --> 00:58:11,696
‎I'll call you when it's time.

702
00:58:13,531 --> 00:58:15,241
‎Okay then.

703
00:58:15,950 --> 00:58:17,452
‎You're heading home now, right?

704
00:58:32,133 --> 00:58:32,967
‎Good night!

705
00:58:33,051 --> 00:58:34,302
‎Good night.

706
00:59:01,037 --> 00:59:02,163
‎What are you doing here?

707
00:59:08,836 --> 00:59:09,671
‎Choi Jeong-yo.

708
00:59:13,341 --> 00:59:14,676
‎Give me another chance.

709
00:59:18,012 --> 00:59:18,930
‎The performance…

710
00:59:20,848 --> 00:59:22,100
‎Let me do it.

711
00:59:26,938 --> 00:59:28,189
‎Don't be ridiculous.

712
00:59:31,776 --> 00:59:32,735
‎That piece.

713
00:59:33,945 --> 00:59:35,738
‎You wrote it out of pure hatred for me.

714
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:37,824
‎Do you really think

715
00:59:38,491 --> 00:59:40,451
‎anyone else can actually play it right?

716
00:59:45,748 --> 00:59:47,166
‎Thanks, Jeong-yo.

717
00:59:48,167 --> 00:59:50,003
‎This experience made me realize my limits.

718
00:59:50,086 --> 00:59:50,962
‎However,

719
00:59:51,671 --> 00:59:53,047
‎when it comes to ‎Nemesis‎,

720
00:59:54,549 --> 00:59:57,051
‎I know no one else
‎can do that piece justice.

721
01:00:00,305 --> 01:00:01,598
‎Will you throw this chance away

722
01:00:02,849 --> 01:00:04,309
‎just for revenge?

723
01:00:35,673 --> 01:00:37,800
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

724
01:00:37,884 --> 01:00:42,096
‎Do you believe flawed artists
‎don't deserve to make art?

725
01:00:42,180 --> 01:00:46,225
‎Or do you believe in
‎separating the art from the artist?

726
01:00:46,309 --> 01:00:49,062
‎Are you trying to play judge,

727
01:00:49,145 --> 01:00:50,772
‎or are you trying to be a musician?

728
01:00:50,855 --> 01:00:54,692
‎If only you had acknowledged him,
‎I wouldn't have done something this crazy!

729
01:00:54,776 --> 01:00:55,610
‎How could you do that?

730
01:00:55,693 --> 01:00:58,154
‎Why aren't you answering?
‎When do I release this?

731
01:00:58,237 --> 01:00:59,822
‎Only I get to mess with him.

732
01:00:59,906 --> 01:01:01,616
‎Just admit it.

733
01:01:01,699 --> 01:01:04,035
‎The only person
‎who can do this piece justice

734
01:01:04,118 --> 01:01:05,328
‎is me.

735
01:01:06,329 --> 01:01:11,334
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
